# draft
// FIRST DRAFT (phase 2): rewrite or sign off. Voice: docs/voice.md. Flags: docs/story-drafts.md.
The dead come in wet today, with salt in their beards and weed in their hair. By the time the queue is in, there's a puddle round your boots.
"Sea battle off the skerries," says Skögul. "The drowned go to Rán. She keeps a net for them, and she doesn't share." # speaker: skogul
"They'll tell you they died with a sword in their hand. Some did, and then fell in. Rán still wants them." # speaker: skogul
She wrings the hem of her cloak out onto the floor of the hall, as a matter of principle.
* ["How do I tell?"]
  "Foam on the lips. The sea leaves its mark on everyone it keeps." # speaker: skogul
* ["Does Rán pay better than Odin?"]
  Skögul snorts.
  "Nobody pays better than Odin. Nobody pays worse, either." # speaker: skogul
  # fx: standing odin -1
- "It isn't only the fleet," she says. "The herring are running. Everyone with a boat is out, and the weather doesn't care who." # speaker: skogul
The first of them is dripping on your table before you've inked the stamp.
-> END
